</head>
<body id="overview">
<header class="topbar"><div class="wrap topline"><a class="brand" href="#overview">TNT <span>NUMERICAL METHODS</span></a><nav class="toplinks" aria-label="Report sections"><a href="#forces">Forces</a><a href="#orbits">Orbits</a><a href="#timings">Timing controls</a><a href="#evidence">Full report</a><a href="#data">Data</a><button type="button" id="print-report">Print / PDF</button></nav></div></header>
<main class="wrap">
<noscript><p class="nojs">JavaScript is disabled. The full written report and scientific figure below remain readable. Enable JavaScript for the interactive comparisons and embedded data downloads.</p></noscript>
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="title"><p class="eyebrow">Orbit integration study · 18 October 2026</p><h1 id="title">Direct forces and<br>interpolated grids</h1><p class="lead">A controlled comparison of force accuracy, retained orbit statistics and CPU runtime, using the same physical galaxy models and Dopri8 integration scheme.</p><div class="protocol"><span>Float64 · Gaussian order 800</span><span>200 reference periods · 50,000 samples</span><span>Two galaxy models · Four orbit launches</span></div><div class="recommendation"><h2>Keep the direct evaluator.</h2><p>Trilinear grids make individual force requests cheaper. At the agreed state tolerance of <code>1e-9</code>, the fine grid requires far more adaptive steps, produces larger physical-energy drift and takes longer to integrate the measured orbits. A smoother interpolation method is a candidate for a future experiment.</p></div><div class="facts"><div class="fact"><strong>≈ 0.026%</strong><span>Largest fine-grid force difference, including along-orbit probes</span></div><div class="fact"><strong>15.5–16.8×</strong><span>Fine-grid adaptive step count relative to direct integration</span></div><div class="fact"><strong>1.40–1.52×</strong><span>Fine-grid whole-solve median time relative to direct, with the protected final-case control</span></div></div></section>
<section id="forces" class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / Force evaluation</p><h2>Accuracy improves as the grid grows.</h2><p>Each model has 4,645 fixed probes, shared by all three resolutions. Differences use vector norms against the direct order-800 evaluator, which is a numerical reference rather than an exact solution.</p></div></div><div class="controls"><label>Galaxy model<select id="geometry"><option value="oblate">Oblate</option><option value="strong_triaxial">Strongly triaxial</option></select></label><label>Radial profile statistic<select id="force-stat"><option value="maximum">Maximum in each radius bin</option><option value="median">Median in each radius bin</option></select></label></div><div class="two"><div class="plot"><h3>Relative force difference across radius</h3><div id="force-profile"></div><p class="note">32 logarithmic radius bins use every probe. Markers are binned summaries; connecting lines guide the eye and do not predict unsampled radii.</p></div><div class="plot"><h3>Cost of sequential force requests</h3><div id="force-runtime"></div><p class="note">Median of three synchronized warm scans, each with 2,048 requests. Grid construction and compilation are excluded here.</p></div></div><div class="legend" aria-label="Evaluator colours"><span><i class="swatch" style="--c:var(--direct)"></i>Direct</span><span><i class="swatch" style="--c:var(--coarse)"></i>Coarse · 80 × 12 × 12</span><span><i class="swatch" style="--c:var(--medium)"></i>Medium · 160 × 24 × 24</span><span><i class="swatch" style="--c:var(--fine)"></i>Fine · 320 × 48 × 48</span></div><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Grid accuracy and per-model setup observations. Warm construction has one observation per grid; these are not confidence intervals.</caption><thead><tr><th>Grid</th><th>Maximum force difference</th><th>99th percentile</th><th>Table size</th><th>Warm construction</th><th>Compilation / lowering</th></tr></thead><tbody id="force-table"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="orbits" class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / Complete orbit solves</p><h2>Cheaper force calls do not guarantee faster orbits.</h2><p>Compare the same launch, clock, random key and output times. Every solve retains the direct physical potential for energy diagnostics.</p></div></div><div class="controls"><label>Orbit launch<select id="orbit-case"></select></label><label>Grid for retained-statistic comparison<select id="grid"><option value="coarse">Coarse</option><option value="medium">Medium</option><option value="fine" selected>Fine</option></select></label><label>Whole-solve timing basis<select id="orbit-timing"><option value="report">Report basis: protected final case</option><option value="original">Original matrix observations</option></select></label></div><p id="orbit-context" class="note" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="two"><div class="plot"><h3>Whole-solve warm median</h3><div id="orbit-runtime"></div></div><div class="plot"><h3>Maximum normalized physical-energy drift</h3><div id="orbit-energy"></div></div></div><p class="note">Energy drift is max |E − E<sub>launch</sub>| / V² at all saved samples and the endpoint. It is neither divided by initial energy nor the solver’s local state tolerance. Timing includes sampling and these energy diagnostics.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Evaluator</th><th>Warm median [range], s</th><th>Max energy drift</th><th>Accepted steps</th><th>Rejected steps</th><th>Total / direct</th></tr></thead><tbody id="orbit-table"></tbody></table></div><h3>Retained intrinsic statistics: selected grid versus direct</h3><div id="retained" class="metric-grid" aria-live="polite"></div><p id="retained-context" class="note"></p><p class="notice">These are raw intrinsic histograms, before spatial symmetries, counter-rotation or observational projection. Total variation is half the summed absolute probability difference. Split-half variation gives finite-window context, not an error bar or an acceptance threshold.</p><div class="actions"><button type="button" id="download-csv">Download this orbit table as CSV</button></div></section>
<section id="timings" class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / Measurement conditions</p><h2>Keep the timing qualification attached.</h2><p>The final triaxial outer-box series contains large wall-time outliers. Host power logs show sleep overlapping late measurements. A separate control repeated that launch under a verified temporary keep-awake assertion.</p></div></div><div class="controls"><label>Timing series for triaxial box E5<select id="timing-series"><option value="awake">Keep-awake, rotated-order control</option><option value="original">Original orbit matrix</option><option value="first">First rotated-order control</option></select></label></div><div class="two"><div class="plot"><h3>All three warm observations and their median</h3><div id="timing-plot"></div><p class="note">Dots are individual observations; the bar is the median. Ranges are measured spreads, not confidence intervals.</p></div><div><h3 id="timing-title"></h3><p id="timing-context" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Evaluator</th><th>Repeat 1</th><th>Repeat 2</th><th>Repeat 3</th><th>Median, s</th></tr></thead><tbody id="timing-table"></tbody></table></div><p class="note">One compiled warmup per method preceded each control’s three rotated-order cycles. Every control solve reproduced its parent trajectory, saved times and diagnostics exactly. All original observations are retained.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="figures" class="section"><p class="eyebrow">04 / Original scientific figure</p><h2>The complete comparison at a glance</h2><figure class="figure"><img id="scientific-figure" src="@@FIGURE@@" width="2340" height="1620" loading="lazy" alt="Four panels show force convergence, sequential request cost, physical-energy drift and whole-orbit runtime. The fine grids have lower force error than coarse grids but much larger energy drift than direct integration and slower full solves."><figcaption>The marked final-case runtime uses the keep-awake timing control. Other orbit timings are from the main matrix. The energy panel uses the original, numerically identical trajectories. All 96 main/control solves succeeded.</figcaption></figure><div class="actions"><button type="button" data-download="comparison.png">Download original PNG</button><button type="button" data-download="comparison.pdf">Download vector PDF</button></div></section>
<section id="evidence" class="section"><p class="eyebrow">05 / Method, limitations and reproduction</p><h2>The full written report travels with this file.</h2><p>The original protocol, all result tables, numerical qualifications, validation record and reproduction commands are included below. The experiment is a benchmark-only prototype, not a production evaluator or a literal DYNAMITE port.</p><details class="complete" id="complete-report"><summary>Open the complete report</summary><article class="report">@@REPORT@@</article></details></section>
<section id="data" class="section data-section"><p class="eyebrow">06 / Embedded evidence</p><h2>Portable data, with the original hashes.</h2><p>The five complete JSON artifacts are embedded as compressed copies. “JSON” restores their exact original bytes; “Gzip” downloads the compressed copy. No data is fetched from a server. Large raw trajectories and grid tables remain outside this document, as described in the written report.</p><p id="decompression-note" class="note"></p><div id="asset-list"></div><div class="actions" style="margin-top:20px"><button type="button" data-download="FORCE_GRID.md">Download source Markdown</button></div><p id="download-status" class="status" role="status"></p><details class="complete"><summary>Asset manifest and SHA-256 hashes</summary><pre>@@MANIFEST@@</pre></details></section>
<footer class="footer"><p>Self-contained research report · Data from 18 October 2026 · CPU, float64, two-vCPU / 4 GB Linux VM.<br>Production remains on the direct static evaluator. A smoother, potential-consistent interpolation method is a future experiment. Parameter gradients, GPU performance and final observable acceptance remain unvalidated.</p><p>All styling, interaction code, report text, figures and portable data are embedded. External source citations open only when selected.</p></footer>
</main>
<div id="tooltip" class="tooltip" role="tooltip" hidden></div>
<script id="report-summary" type="application/json">@@SUMMARY@@</script>
<script id="report-assets" type="application/json">@@ASSETS@@</script>
<script>
'use strict';
const D=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('report-summary').textContent);
const ASSETS=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('report-assets').textContent);
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);
const methods=['direct','coarse','medium','fine'];
const colours={direct:'#234e70',coarse:'#ae6410',medium:'#35774f',fine:'#a3434d'};
const names={direct:'Direct',coarse:'Coarse',medium:'Medium',fine:'Fine'};
const caseName=id=>id.replace('strong_triaxial','Triaxial').replace('oblate','Oblate').replaceAll('-',' ');
const fmt=(v,d=2)=>Number(v).toLocaleString('en-GB',{minimumFractionDigits:d,maximumFractionDigits:d});
const sci=v=>Number(v).toExponential(2);
const percent=v=>fmt(v*100,3)+'%';
const median=values=>[...values].sort((a,b)=>a-b)[Math.floor(values.length/2)];
const rangeText=values=>`${fmt(median(values))} [${fmt(Math.min(...values))}–${fmt(Math.max(...values))}]`;
const escape=s=>String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
const tip=$('tooltip');
function showTip(event,text){tip.textContent=text;tip.hidden=false;const r=event.target.getBoundingClientRect();const x=event.clientX||r.left+r.width/2,y=event.clientY||r.top;tip.style.left=Math.max(8,Math.min(innerWidth-tip.offsetWidth-8,x+12))+'px';tip.style.top=Math.max(8,Math.min(innerHeight-tip.offsetHeight-8,y+12))+'px';}
function hideTip(){tip.hidden=true;}
function svgEl(tag,attrs={},text){const el=document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg',tag);for(const[k,v]of Object.entries(attrs))el.setAttribute(k,v);if(text!==undefined)el.textContent=text;return el;}
function text(svg,x,y,label,attrs={}){svg.append(svgEl('text',{x,y,...attrs},label));}
function mark(svg,node,description){node.setAttribute('tabindex','0');node.setAttribute('aria-label',description);node.addEventListener('pointermove',e=>showTip(e,description));node.addEventListener('focus',e=>showTip(e,description));node.addEventListener('pointerleave',hideTip);node.addEventListener('blur',hideTip);node.addEventListener('click',e=>showTip(e,description));svg.append(node);}
function chartBase(id,title,yLabel){const host=$(id),w=Math.max(280,host.clientWidth),h=300;host.replaceChildren();const svg=svgEl('svg',{viewBox:`0 0 ${w} ${h}`,role:'img','aria-label':title});svg.append(svgEl('title',{},title));host.append(svg);const f={svg,w,h,l:72,r:w-16,t:18,b:238};text(svg,15,130,yLabel,{transform:'rotate(-90 15 130)','text-anchor':'middle'});return f;}
function bars(id,rows,title,yLabel,options={}){const f=chartBase(id,title,yLabel),{svg,l,r,t,b}=f;const vals=rows.flatMap(row=>options.points?row.points:[row.value]);const log=Boolean(options.log);const lo=log?10**Math.floor(Math.log10(Math.min(...vals))):0;const hi=log?10**Math.ceil(Math.log10(Math.max(...vals))):Math.max(...vals)*1.25;const Y=v=>log?b-(Math.log10(v)-Math.log10(lo))/(Math.log10(hi)-Math.log10(lo))*(b-t):b-v/hi*(b-t);
 const ticks=log?Array.from({length:Math.log10(hi/lo)+1},(_,i)=>lo*10**i):Array.from({length:5},(_,i)=>hi*i/4);
 for(const v of ticks){const y=Y(v);svg.append(svgEl('line',{x1:l,x2:r,y1:y,y2:y,class:'grid'}));text(svg,l-8,y+4,log?v.toExponential(0):fmt(v,hi<1?2:1),{'text-anchor':'end'});}
 const slot=(r-l)/rows.length,bw=Math.min(50,slot*.54);rows.forEach((row,i)=>{const x=l+slot*(i+.5),y=Y(row.value);const label=`${row.label}: ${log?sci(row.value):fmt(row.value,3)} ${options.unit||''}${row.points?'\nWarm observations: '+row.points.map(v=>fmt(v,3)).join(', '):''}`;mark(svg,svgEl('rect',{x:x-bw/2,y,width:bw,height:Math.max(1,b-y),fill:colours[row.key],opacity:options.selected && row.key!==options.selected ? 0.55 : 0.95}),label);if(slot>70||!log)text(svg,x,Math.max(t+11,y-7),log?sci(row.value):fmt(row.value,2),{'text-anchor':'middle',class:'bar-value'});text(svg,x,b+22,row.label,{'text-anchor':'middle'});if(options.points)row.points.forEach((v,j)=>mark(svg,svgEl('circle',{cx:x+(j-1)*7,cy:Y(v),r:4,fill:'#fff',stroke:colours[row.key],'stroke-width':2}),`${row.label}, repeat ${j+1}: ${fmt(v,3)} s`));});
 svg.append(svgEl('line',{x1:l,x2:r,y1:b,y2:b,class:'axis'}));text(svg,(l+r)/2,286,'Evaluator',{'text-anchor':'middle'});}
function profile(){const geometry=$('geometry').value,stat=$('force-stat').value;const rows=D.forces.filter(x=>x.geometry===geometry&&x.variant!=='direct');const f=chartBase('force-profile','Relative force difference by radius','Relative force difference (%)');const{svg,l,r,t,b}=f;const points=rows.flatMap(x=>x.profile);const xmin=Math.min(...points.map(x=>x.lower)),xmax=Math.max(...points.map(x=>x.upper));const min=Math.min(...points.map(x=>x[stat]*100)),max=Math.max(...points.map(x=>x[stat]*100));const ymin=10**Math.floor(Math.log10(min)),ymax=10**Math.ceil(Math.log10(max));const X=v=>l+(Math.log10(v/xmin)/Math.log10(xmax/xmin))*(r-l);const Y=v=>b-Math.log10(v/ymin)/Math.log10(ymax/ymin)*(b-t);const yPowers=Math.round(Math.log10(ymax/ymin)),stride=Math.max(1,Math.ceil(yPowers/5));for(let i=0;i<=yPowers;i+=stride){const v=ymin*10**i,y=Y(v);svg.append(svgEl('line',{x1:l,x2:r,y1:y,y2:y,class:'grid'}));text(svg,l-8,y+4,v.toExponential(0),{'text-anchor':'end'});}for(const v of (f.w<440?[1e-5,1e-2,1e1]:[1e-5,1e-3,1e-1,1e1,2e2])){const x=X(v);text(svg,x,b+22,v.toExponential(0),{'text-anchor':x>r-15?'end':x<l+10?'start':'middle'});}rows.forEach(row=>{svg.append(svgEl('path',{d:row.profile.map((v,i)=>`${i?'L':'M'}${X(v.radius)},${Y(v[stat]*100)}`).join(' '),fill:'none',stroke:colours[row.variant],'stroke-width':2}));row.profile.forEach(v=>mark(svg,svgEl('circle',{cx:X(v.radius),cy:Y(v[stat]*100),r:3.5,fill:colours[row.variant]}),`${names[row.variant]} · ${stat} within radius bin\n${sci(v.lower)}–${sci(v.upper)} kpc · ${v.count} probes\nRelative force difference: ${percent(v[stat])}`));});svg.append(svgEl('line',{x1:l,x2:r,y1:b,y2:b,class:'axis'}));text(svg,(l+r)/2,286,'Radius (kpc, logarithmic scale)',{'text-anchor':'middle'});
 const all=D.forces.filter(x=>x.geometry===geometry);bars('force-runtime',all.map(x=>({key:x.variant,label:names[x.variant],value:x.serial_timing.warm_median_seconds*1000})),'Sequential force request timings','Milliseconds / 2,048 requests',{unit:'ms'});$('force-table').innerHTML=rows.map(x=>`<tr><td>${names[x.variant]}</td><td>${percent(x.error.max_relative)}</td><td>${percent(x.error.p99_relative)}</td><td>${fmt(x.setup.table_bytes/1048576,3)} MiB</td><td>${fmt(x.setup.warm_reconstruction_seconds,3)} s</td><td>${fmt(x.setup.lowering_and_compilation_seconds,3)} s</td></tr>`).join('');}
function orbitRows(){return D.orbits.filter(x=>x.case_id===$('orbit-case').value);}
function orbitTimes(row){return $('orbit-timing').value==='report'&&row.case_id===D.protectedCase?D.awake[row.variant].warm_seconds:row.warm_seconds;}
function orbits(){const rows=orbitRows(),selected=$('grid').value,direct=rows.find(x=>x.variant==='direct');const protectedTiming=$('orbit-timing').value==='report'&&direct.case_id===D.protectedCase;$('orbit-context').textContent=`${caseName(direct.case_id)} · ${protectedTiming?'Protected, rotated-order timing control.':direct.case_id===D.protectedCase?'Original timing series: host-sleep confound; see the timing controls.':'Original orbit matrix timings.'} Three warm observations per evaluator.`;bars('orbit-runtime',rows.map(x=>({key:x.variant,label:names[x.variant],value:median(orbitTimes(x))})),'Whole-orbit warm median','Seconds',{selected,unit:'s'});bars('orbit-energy',rows.map(x=>({key:x.variant,label:names[x.variant],value:x.diagnostics.max_energy_error})),'Maximum normalized physical-energy drift','Max |E − E launch| / V²',{selected,log:true});$('orbit-table').innerHTML=rows.map(x=>`<tr class="${x.variant===selected?'selected':''}"><td>${names[x.variant]}</td><td>${rangeText(orbitTimes(x))}</td><td>${sci(x.diagnostics.max_energy_error)}</td><td>${x.diagnostics.num_accepted_steps.toLocaleString('en-GB')}</td><td>${x.diagnostics.num_rejected_steps.toLocaleString('en-GB')}</td><td>${fmt(x.diagnostics.num_steps/direct.diagnostics.num_steps)}×</td></tr>`).join('');const c=D.controls.find(x=>x.case_id===direct.case_id&&x.working_vs===selected),v=c.distribution_difference;$('retained').innerHTML=[['Radial total variation',percent(v.radial_tv)],['Spatial total variation',percent(v.spatial_tv)],['Maximum velocity TV',percent(Math.max(...v.velocity_tv))],['Second-moment difference / V²',sci(v.second_moment_max_abs)]].map(([k,val])=>`<div><span>${k}</span><strong>${val}</strong></div>`).join('');$('retained-context').textContent=`${names[selected]} versus direct. Direct spatial split-half variation: ${percent(direct.split_half_variation.spatial_tv)}. First-period position RMS / L: ${sci(c.first_period_position_rms_over_L)}; velocity RMS / V: ${sci(c.first_period_velocity_rms_over_V)}.`;}
function timing(){const source=$('timing-series').value,original=D.orbits.filter(x=>x.case_id===D.protectedCase);const rows=methods.map(key=>({key,label:names[key],points:source==='original'?original.find(x=>x.variant===key).warm_seconds:(source==='awake'?D.awake:D.timing)[key].warm_seconds}));rows.forEach(x=>x.value=median(x.points));bars('timing-plot',rows,'Individual warm timings for triaxial box E5','Seconds',{points:true,unit:'s'});$('timing-table').innerHTML=rows.map(x=>`<tr><td>${x.label}</td>${x.points.map(v=>`<td>${fmt(v)}</td>`).join('')}<td>${fmt(x.value)}</td></tr>`).join('');$('timing-title').textContent=source==='awake'?'Protected host conditions':source==='original'?'Original matrix observations':'First rotated-order control';$('timing-context').textContent=source==='awake'?'A temporary keep-awake assertion was verified before and after this run, with no new host sleep event. No permanent power or VM setting changed. Remaining spread still reflects machine-state variability.':'These observations overlap a period in which host power logs recorded sleep. They are preserved in full, but are not interpreted as isolated CPU performance measurements. The cause of each outlier is not fully isolated.';}
function saveBlob(blob,name){const a=document.createElement('a'),url=URL.createObjectURL(blob);a.href=url;a.download=name;document.body.append(a);a.click();a.remove();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),30000);}
async function download(name,compressed=false){try{const asset=ASSETS[name];if(!asset)throw Error('Unknown embedded asset.');let raw;if(asset.encoding==='figure')raw=Uint8Array.from(atob($('scientific-figure').src.split(',')[1]),c=>c.charCodeAt(0));else raw=Uint8Array.from(atob(asset.base64),c=>c.charCodeAt(0));let blob=new Blob([raw],{type:compressed?'application/gzip':asset.mime||'image/png'});if(asset.encoding==='gzip'&&!compressed){if(!('DecompressionStream'in window))throw Error('JSON decompression is unavailable in this browser. Use the explicitly labelled Gzip copy.');const stream=blob.stream().pipeThrough(new DecompressionStream('gzip'));blob=await new Response(stream).blob();}saveBlob(blob,name+(compressed?'.gz':''));$('download-status').textContent=`Downloaded ${name}${compressed?'.gz':''}.`;}catch(error){$('download-status').textContent=error.message;$('download-status').setAttribute('role','alert');}}
function assetList(){const json=Object.values(ASSETS).filter(x=>x.mime==='application/json');$('asset-list').innerHTML=json.map(x=>`<div class="asset"><div><h3>${escape(x.name)}</h3><small>${fmt(x.bytes/1048576,3)} MiB uncompressed · SHA-256 ${escape(x.sha256)}</small></div><div class="actions"><button type="button" data-download="${x.name}" ${'DecompressionStream'in window?'':'disabled'}>JSON</button><button type="button" data-download="${x.name}" data-compressed="true">Gzip</button></div></div>`).join('');$('decompression-note').textContent='DecompressionStream'in window?'This browser can restore the original JSON files directly. Gzip copies are also available.':'This browser lacks native gzip decompression. The report and charts work; download the labelled Gzip copies to extract the original JSON with a gzip tool.';}
document.addEventListener('click',e=>{const target=e.target.closest('[data-download]');if(target){e.preventDefault();download(target.dataset.download,target.dataset.compressed==='true');}});
$('print-report').addEventListener('click',()=>window.print());let opened=[];addEventListener('beforeprint',()=>{opened=[...document.querySelectorAll('details')].filter(x=>x.open);document.querySelectorAll('details').forEach(x=>x.open=true);});addEventListener('afterprint',()=>document.querySelectorAll('details').forEach(x=>x.open=opened.includes(x)));
$('orbit-case').innerHTML=D.cases.map(x=>`<option value="${escape(x.id)}">${escape(caseName(x.id))}</option>`).join('');
['geometry','force-stat'].forEach(id=>$(id).addEventListener('change',()=>{hideTip();profile();}));['orbit-case','grid','orbit-timing'].forEach(id=>$(id).addEventListener('change',()=>{hideTip();orbits();}));$('timing-series').addEventListener('change',()=>{hideTip();timing();});
$('download-csv').addEventListener('click',()=>{const lines=[['case','evaluator','timing_basis','warm_median_s','warm_1_s','warm_2_s','warm_3_s','max_energy_error_over_V2','accepted_steps','rejected_steps']];for(const r of orbitRows()){const t=orbitTimes(r);lines.push([r.case_id,r.variant,$('orbit-timing').selectedOptions[0].text,median(t),...t,r.diagnostics.max_energy_error,r.diagnostics.num_accepted_steps,r.diagnostics.num_rejected_steps]);}saveBlob(new Blob([lines.map(row=>row.map(x=>'"'+String(x).replaceAll('"','""')+'"').join(',')).join('\r\n')],{type:'text/csv;charset=utf-8'}),'orbit-comparison.csv');});
let resizeTimer;addEventListener('resize',()=>{clearTimeout(resizeTimer);resizeTimer=setTimeout(()=>{hideTip();profile();orbits();timing();},100);});
assetList();profile();orbits();timing();
</script>
</body>
</html>
